{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be","id":929121,"title":"If you were to live in the classic WOD.. What supernatural would you choose to be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-10T02:06:14-07:00","id":929121,"title":"If you were to live in the classic WOD.. What supernatural would you choose to be?","content":"Vampire<br /> Kuei-jin<br /> Changeling<br /> Fera (if so which one)<br /> Garou<br /> <br /> <br /> No mage because they are really op.<br /> <br /> You start off fresh into the WOD. What would your goals be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1945,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","user":"Magicballz","date":". 07-10-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T09:24:25-07:00","id":929249,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of wondering what world one lives in where one looks at Mummy and Demon powers and thinks &quot;Yeah these things aren't OP but mages.. that's crazy talk&quot; Now if your point is &quot;no mages because they are the obvious choice because no real down side to being a mage&quot; that's far fairer.. but serious Mummies and Demons aren't anywehere near the same situation as the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T09:59:33-07:00","id":929258,"title":"","content":"Imbued Defender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T13:17:52-07:00","id":929361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929249#post929249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of wondering what world one lives in where one looks at Mummy and Demon powers and thinks &quot;Yeah these things aren't OP but mages.. that's crazy talk&quot; Now if your point is &quot;no mages because they are the obvious choice because no real down side to being a mage&quot; that's far fairer.. but serious Mummies and Demons aren't anywehere near the same situation as the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean aren't anywhere near the same situation as the others. Can you explain more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T14:18:23-07:00","id":929378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929361#post929361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean aren't anywhere near the same situation as the others. Can you explain more.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Demons and Mummies aren't as game-breakingly powerful as Mages, they are still up there.<br /> <br /> Demon for example has quite a few lores that allow you to steamroll social interactions, deal massive amounts of bashing, lethal or aggrevated damage, lock people in places they can't escape from, warp a person's body to the point of uselessness, see the future, throw all subtlety out the window and cause massive damage or just outright kill a roomfull of people with a single use of one of your powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:17:08-07:00","id":929408,"title":"","content":"I think it would be nice to be a Gurahl. The ritualistic behavior and the healing capabilities would be nice. Other than that, a Mokole would be quite fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:41:26-07:00","id":929421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929378#post929378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Demons and Mummies aren't as game-breakingly powerful as Mages, they are still up there.<br /> <br /> Demon for example has quite a few lores that allow you to steamroll social interactions, deal massive amounts of bashing, lethal or aggrevated damage, lock people in places they can't escape from, warp a person's body to the point of uselessness, see the future, throw all subtlety out the window and cause massive damage or just outright kill a roomfull of people with a single use of one of your powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This plus they get to build theirown killing machine form. That gets better the more kewl powerz they get.<br /> <br /> Mummies have insane abuses at the Pcish level like cast Final fantasy Meteor, erase someone from existance, plus they are innately almost impossible to put down, have blood that either grants humanity or agg damage to a vampire.. if we put WoD characters in Tiers Demon and Mummy are up there with mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:18:51-07:00","id":929441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929421#post929421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This plus they get to build theirown killing machine form. That gets better the more kewl powerz they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. Sure, there's a lot of fun stuff to be had from the DIY Apocalypse Form thing but it ain't exactly on par with a Crinos form. Sure, there are a few extremly powerful things in there like a Slayer hitting someone with Touch of Death (by keeping in physical contact a person cannot act at all), a high-Torment Devourer with Toxins and Gaping Maw can do a LOT of damage real quick (Oh, you can soak lethal damage? Please soak 12 of it.) and a high-Faith Defiler with Shocking Touch can take an unsuspecting target out of the fight fast. Zap.<br /> <br /> But like I said, there is a lot of funn stuff in there but because of the limits regarding the form you'll be hard-pressed to use these powers all the time. Oh, and if you want to function at full power you'll either take a hit in Torment or have it be very high to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:31:42-07:00","id":929444,"title":"","content":"I'd hate being a vampire because it's evil but who wouldn't want to be a Toreador?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:44:14-07:00","id":929449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929444#post929444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd hate being a vampire because it's evil but who wouldn't want to be a Toreador?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Nosferatu, for one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:44:37-07:00","id":929451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929441#post929441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not entirely. Sure, there's a lot of fun stuff to be had from the DIY Apocalypse Form thing but it ain't exactly on par with a Crinos form. Sure, there are a few extremly powerful things in there like a Slayer hitting someone with Touch of Death (by keeping in physical contact a person cannot act at all), a high-Torment Devourer with Toxins and Gaping Maw can do a LOT of damage real quick (Oh, you can soak lethal damage? Please soak 12 of it.) and a high-Faith Defiler with Shocking Touch can take an unsuspecting target out of the fight fast. Zap.<br /> <br /> But like I said, there is a lot of funn stuff in there but because of the limits regarding the form you'll be hard-pressed to use these powers all the time. Oh, and if you want to function at full power you'll either take a hit in Torment or have it be very high to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apocalypse form isn't Crinos.. but its more than the Nothing whatsoever you get as a mage. Its a free benefit you get for raising your powers. Lores by themselves are pretty close to spheres. Over all Demons get to sit in the same section as Mages and Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:03:08-07:00","id":929456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929449#post929449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Nosferatu, for one.</div> </div> </div> </div>They just hate us because we're beautiful.<br /> <br /> *the geeky bearded nerd sips his cola*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:51:15-07:00","id":929466,"title":"","content":"I see. Well I think you would want to consider the consequences of being a mummy or demon. Just for balance sake I will remove them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:43:31-07:00","id":929480,"title":"","content":"I actually think that Mummies may be more powerful than Mages. I think that a Mummy can erase a Mage from existence much easier than a Mage can do the same for them. And Mummies come back from the dead, which kind of makes them cooler than practically everyone else. While I like Shapeshifters more than Mummies, Mummies are kind of on top of the pile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T05:21:42-07:00","id":929668,"title":"","content":"between those 5 i would choose to become a vampire blood mage. as for clan... maybe an indian ventrue(called danava i think) though in the long run it doesn't matter<br /> <br /> vampires are the most powerful supernaturals of those mentioned. granted they may not start so but they do become in the long long run,<br /> <br /> likewise vampiric weakness up to and including sunlight are beaten up in the long long LONG run.<br /> <br /> fera may start powerful but there is a limit to how powerful they may get. also they are not naturally immortal and many of their gifts/power seem to depend on the cooperation of spirits.<br /> <br /> while i don't know much about changelings they seem very weak(now changelings from dark ages fae are another story entirely)<br /> <br /> kuei jin are indeed quite strong but from what i know of them their sorcery seems weaker than blood magic . at any rate even if they are equal i just like western vampires more<br /> <br /> imbued suck. not only do they not have any innate powers but many of their edges are only useful against the supernatural and just not &quot;practical&quot; in an everyday sense. plus there is this whole messenger and madness thing.<br /> <br /> wraiths suck because of this whole &quot;you are an immaterial ghost thing&quot; now granted if you are a ferryman or just abuse the rules to give yourself similar powers things improve quite a bit. especially given how cheap arcanoi are;. but you still don't quite reach the level of vampire blood mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:57:08-07:00","id":929871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929421#post929421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummies have insane abuses at the Pcish level like cast Final fantasy Meteor, <b>erase someone from existance</b>[...]</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929480#post929480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a Mummy can <b>erase</b> a Mage <b>from existence</b> much easier than a Mage can do the same for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guys. C'mon. Context. Forgetting the Person is a Level 5 Nomenclature ritual rolled at difficulty 9 and requires 30 Sekhem, and sacrifices a permanent dot of Balance. It has a pretty high cost for Amenti.<br /> <br /> But back on topic. For me? Risen. I love ghost stories, I like vampires, and risen often have (vengeance-related) goals that are clearly defined.<br /> <br /> Plus, <i>The Crow</i> had a cool soundtrack.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:54:14-07:00","id":929911,"title":"","content":"I'd be a Nuwisha. No rage, just a powerful hankering to deliver Momma Gaia's justice via painful hijinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:36:52-07:00","id":929941,"title":"","content":"Nuwisha are cool, though I think that any of the Fera could be considered to be fairly awesome, though I think that the Corax and Kitsune are probably the least cool (both of them having breeding difficulties and the Kitsune have no Delirium and no Regeneration). Ratkin are often overlooked though because of their larger cousins. I could imagine that a game involving an entire high school filled with Homid Ratkin adolescents who were 'rescued' by the government after surviving by the Birthing Plague could be rather awesome (one thousand losers suddenly transformed by the power of Rat into superheroes!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:05:59-07:00","id":929956,"title":"","content":"My first choice would a Same-bito wereshark. Immortality (without sacrificing something like Vampires), plus I'd be able to hang out on land or under the sea. Nearly the best of all worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:23:04-07:00","id":929965,"title":"","content":"I'd be a Garou--preferably something that aligns with my social politics (so, Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, or Black Furies--though I am a man), and my profession (I'm an attorney, so philodox or ragabash).<br /> <br /> Garou have community, friendship, brotherhood, a worthy cause to fight for, and an indisputable and unapologetically evil foe to fight. A Garou can expect to marry and have children, and even if they're suuuuuper unlikely to die of old age, their deaths at least have some meaning. Furthermore, their spirits &quot;go&quot; somewhere after they die--whether to be reincarnated or to Garou heaven (the Summer Country, no?), and further, the Garou have about as close and personal a relationship with the objects of their religious worship (Gaia and their totems) as one could ever hope to have as a mundane human.<br /> <br /> Given how awful and bleak the World of Darkness is, there's something to be said for having the opportunity to go down fighting, singing, loving, and (sometimes) laughing, in the company of family/friends/neighbors--and not only that, to know that not only is death not the end, but that you're not damned (like a vampire).<br /> <br /> EDIT: I guess unlike a lot of other people upthread, I would never want to live forever, let alone outlive all of my loved ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T15:46:09-07:00","id":930005,"title":"","content":"I think I want to mention is that you have to live as that supernaturals.<br /> <br /> For example, becoming a Kuei-jin is cool but it is implied that the character went to Hell. What experiences said person experienced in Yomi is probably unspeakable horror. If a Kuei-jin died wouldn't he/she return to Yomi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T16:29:52-07:00","id":930027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=929871#post929871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys. C'mon. Context. Forgetting the Person is a Level 5 Nomenclature ritual rolled at difficulty 9 and requires 30 Sekhem, and sacrifices a permanent dot of Balance. It has a pretty high cost for Amenti.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compared to Obfuscate 5 where you can hide a bunch of people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:15:05-07:00","id":930070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=930027#post930027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compared to Obfuscate 5 where you can hide a bunch of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not comparing it to Obfuscate 5. I'm not comparing it to any Discipline, Gift, Sphere, or anything else. I'm pointing out that it is not as easy and simple as it has so far been presented in this thread. Every use of Forgetting the Person costs the Amenti a <i>permanent point</i> of Balance. Hekau and Sekhem are limited by Balance, Attributes and Abilities over 5 are limited by Balance. Every time an Amenti uses Forgetting the Person, the Mummy willingly handicaps herself - and if the Amenti uses it when she only has a Balance of 5, she can't use it again until she raises her Balance, which requires going before the Judges, which requires that she <b><i>dies</i></b>.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:41:21-07:00","id":930091,"title":"","content":"Interesting that people here consider mages overpowered--in the Mage forum there's a recent thread about how to help mages keep up with other splats in mixed games. I tend to come down on the mages are powerful side, but <i>overpowered </i>seems like a bit of a stretch.<br /> <br /> I would definitely have to go with Changeling. While all the options end ultimately in sorrow, the non-Changeling options consist of heavily inhuman and simplified emotions or lives of constant violence--or miserable isolation in the case of most non-lupine changers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 07-11-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T20:47:42-07:00","id":930148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=930091#post930091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting that people here consider mages overpowered--in the Mage forum there's a recent thread about how to help mages keep up with other splats in mixed games. I tend to come down on the mages are powerful side, but <i>overpowered </i>seems like a bit of a stretch.<br /> <br /> I would definitely have to go with Changeling. While all the options end ultimately in sorrow, the non-Changeling options consist of heavily inhuman and simplified emotions or lives of constant violence--or miserable isolation in the case of most non-lupine changers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Power in the world of Darkness is bringing Rocks when your Enemies bring Scissors. Mages have a pretty good toolset for bringing something the otherside just has nothing on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:33:30-07:00","id":930206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=930148#post930148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power in the world of Darkness is bringing Rocks when your Enemies bring Scissors. Mages have a pretty good toolset for bringing something the otherside just has nothing on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably true of mages as a group. But single mage can't hope to cover enough ground to expect to be able to counter everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T03:12:20-07:00","id":930264,"title":"","content":"Mages are like the Batman of World of Darkness. With the proper equipment, spheres and some prep time they can handle just about anything, but without it they're sitting ducks for the physically more menacing critters out there.<br /> <br /> Plus, it also depends on their way of doing magic. Sure, a Dreamspeaker can talk to the spirits of the land to figure out plot stuff and a Hermetic wizard needs to set up magic circles and stuff to get magic done. On the other hand you can have Etherites with guns that shoot burning slugs of silver or a Virtual Adept that has constructed a gun that opens a portal between it and the sun, allowing it to shoot sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T05:50:32-07:00","id":930291,"title":"","content":"I&quot;d be a dhampir. First level disciplines are sweet, but subtle. Lifespan in the order of centuries. The ability to shrug off injury like it was a joke - and I,d never *need* to have a vampire domitor to feed me.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's still the option for embrace later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T09:18:03-07:00","id":930374,"title":"","content":"Nuwisha because garous are too serious<br /> Demon: funny nough, would be independant, trying to use my lores for self gain<br /> Hunter judge or redeemer<br /> <br /> And...would date a changeling chick, likely a pookah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:52:05-07:00","id":930453,"title":"","content":"It would depend on which era of the WOD we are talking about. Close to Gehenna/the Apocalypse or further away. But rokea, mokole or gurahal for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T15:48:16-07:00","id":930562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/929121-if-you-were-to-live-in-the-classic-wod-what-supernatural-would-you-choose-to-be?p=930206#post930206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably true of mages as a group. But single mage can't hope to cover enough ground to expect to be able to counter everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also true, but mages do have a good chance of pulling out something you haven't planned for even if they aren't throwing around all 9 spheres. I mean MIND Alone lets you do everything in PResence, Dominate. Auspex and much of Dementation and you can do stuff on top of that on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T16:31:56-07:00","id":930579,"title":"","content":"I would not mind being an orphaned Dhampyr. With Asian immigration over the last 150 years being as it is, there would have probably been a few dozen Kuei-jin who decided that exile in the New World was preferable to death in the Old World. One Yang-imbalanced male Kuei-jin could have easily sired four children a year on different women, meaning that hundreds could exist in the USA alone. With Passive Joss and a Joss Pool, you could be an action hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T19:35:52-07:00","id":930656,"title":"","content":"Probably a vampire because I have something of an obsession with them. Though being a demon would be pretty sweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T23:46:42-07:00","id":930735,"title":"","content":"Wait, were dhampyrs an option? So far that's the only thing allowed that might actually be an improvement over being human. For me the question is &quot;which awful curse is the least awful,&quot; and from what I remember dhampyrs don't have one, they're just like ghouls but without the blood bond. So basically more awesome and much longer-lived humans. The downside, as other people alluded to, is if you're not orphaned you have a parent that is very powerful and immortal. That combined with East Asian filial piety, and perhaps it can be thought of as a blood bond of similar strength as the Cainite one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 07-13-2016, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T03:56:49-07:00","id":930763,"title":"","content":"Dhampirs can also go out into the sun right?<br /> <br /> Being a Dhampyr would be nice. You also get to use coool powers like a Kuei-Jin too right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"